# Docker Sandboxes web dashboard (agentic-platform.docker.com): the API it calls. Captured 30 Oct 2026, one capture.
# sbx v0.50.0 on the same account. Method: docs/ui-api-capture-method.md. Shapes only: every value is replaced by its
# type ("string", "int64-string", "timestamp", "boolean"), except enum constants, which are kept. No ids, tokens,
# cookies, names or account data. The raw HAR stayed on the capturing machine and is not in this repository.
#
# Transport: POST https://agentic-platform.docker.com/api/<package>.v1.<Service>/<Method>, JSON body, Connect
# protocol (header connect-protocol-version), Authorization: Bearer. Protobuf JSON mapping: int64 as strings, empty
# lists omitted. This is not the published REST API (/v1/..., 42 paths, sbx-api-surface-2026-10-30.log).
#
# Live probe (15:38 UTC): `sbx --cloud create shell --name rpc-probe --cpus 1 --memory 2g`; the dashboard's sandbox
# page opened; Pause clicked; Delete clicked and confirmed. It lived a few minutes on the smallest size.
#   GetSandbox: status=ready while state=running (two fields); expiresAt - createdAt = 60 min; onTimeout=hibernate;
#     autoResume=true; platform=linux/amd64; sandboxVmSize=SANDBOX_VM_SIZE_CPU1_MEM2.
#   GetSandbox.metadata: six provider API-key names, each value the literal placeholder "proxy-managed" (credentials
#     are injected by the proxy; no secret is returned).
#   Pause in the dashboard calls HibernateSandbox; `sbx ls --cloud` then showed "stopping" for about 20 s, then
#     "stopped"; Delete is disabled while stopping. The page then offers "Restore to connect".
#   DeleteSandbox returns {} at once; the next ListSandboxes returned 0 sandboxes, `sbx ls --cloud` "No sandboxes found".
#     A deleted sandbox leaves no record in either list.
#   Request bodies: every per-sandbox method takes {"sandboxId": string}; ListSandboxes takes {"limit": int}, no
#     pageToken or filter seen.
#
# Methods: decoded from the protobuf descriptors embedded in the 89 JavaScript chunks the visited pages loaded.
# Chunks of pages not visited may hold more. Methods seen on the wire but missing from the decoded list
# (HibernateSandbox, DeleteSandbox, CreateSandboxTerminalToken, GetSandboxMCPServers, GetBillingSummary,
# GetPromotionalCreditStatus, ListCommunityKits, ListUserMCPServers, GetHostedMCPEndpoint) confirm that the decoded list
# is incomplete. Not seen anywhere: a create-sandbox method, any streaming method, events, stats, metrics, history,
# quota.
#
# Not captured: the response shapes of GetBillingSummary and GetPromotionalCreditStatus (seen in the first capture,
# not re-read); create from the dashboard; an exec or process call.
